One thing that I suggest to make this even better is to keep this current implementation of DataSource.query for internal use since TypeORM depends on this. Probably through a parameter -- I would trigger sqlite3.all from external calls and keep the user results RAW as expected...

I can actually run this extra bareback/raw in the following way. This took me a few days to track down, so you geniuses may want to stick it in the beginner documentation:
[(Uses FlatPromise to promisify the callback.)](https://www.npmjs.com/package/flat-promise)

```typescript
this.DB = new DataSource(...);
const queryRunner = this.DB.createQueryRunner();

// This is a RAW sqlite3 connection from a possible pool(unlikely).
this.connection = await queryRunner.connect();

const resultPromise = new FlatPromise();
await this
  .connection
  .all(
    statement.query,
    statement.params,
    (err: any, rows: any) => {
      if (err) {
        resultPromise.reject(err);
        return;
      }

      resultPromise.resolve(rows);
    }
);
const result = await resultPromise.promise;
```

The API for sqlite3 is here: https://github.com/TryGhost/node-sqlite3/wiki/API
